  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MMR100252 - EQR DEC Collective Initiatives - DD Passporting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Collective Initiative proposes the development of a Myanmar Aid Passporting Solution (MAPS) to address a key constraint in humanitarian response: duplicative and time-consuming due diligence (DD) processes for local partners. In Myanmar&#x2019;s complex context&#x2014;where over 3.5 million people are displaced and local organisations are central to delivery&#x2014;repeated DD requirements delay partnerships, slow funding, and reduce the timeliness of life-saving assistance._x000d_
_x000d_
Led by World Vision with ActionAid, Plan International and Tearfund, the project will co-create a context-specific DD passporting system that enables INGOs to recognise existing partner assessments. This will streamline onboarding, reduce administrative burden, and promote more equitable partnerships with local and national NGOs. The approach is consultative and grounded in engagement with local actors to ensure relevance to Myanmar&#x2019;s legal, operational, and access constraints._x000d_
_x000d_
Core components include: mapping global DD models and Myanmar requirements; inclusive stakeholder consultations; development of a practical passporting framework with SOPs and data-sharing protocols; capacity strengthening for local NGOs; and pilot and roll-out across participating agencies._x000d_
_x000d_
Aligned with DEC&#x2019;s objective to drive system-level change, the initiative aims to enable faster, more accountable, and locally led humanitarian response. While focused on the INGO&#x2013;local NGO interface, it provides a foundation for future donor alignment and scale-up across contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
